hello everyone I recently returned from  the world government summit in Dubai  where I was pleased to launch a  partnership between the United Arab  Emirates and the World Bank Group to  host an annual platform for education in  this rapidly changing world children  need to be critical thinkers who develop  a lifelong thirst for knowledge and  problem-solving teachers are the heroes  who can equip them to seek analyze and  effectively use information in this  interconnected world children need to  experience and understand other cultures  teachers can play a critical role in  promoting respect and understanding  helping them become better citizens we  know that nothing is possible without  our teachers those of you on the front  line working tirelessly every day to  give our children a brighter future at  the World Bank Group we recognize the  transformational role that teachers play  in shaping children's lives that's why  we support the recruitment and training  of teachers everywhere from India to  Tanzania from Pakistan to Mongolia I've  been lucky to have some great teachers  throughout my life from Elementary  School in the Midwest of the United  States to my professors in medical  school in graduate school I still  remember the lessons I learned from many  committed inspired educators I remain  grateful to all of them I'd like to  extend my gratitude to His Highness  Sheikh Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum  thank you for your support of the  teaching profession the patronage of  this prize and your continued efforts to  promote peace and tolerance many thanks  also to the Varkey foundation for your  commitment to education in every corner  of the world it is my honor and pleasure  to announce the ten finalists for the  2017 global teachers prize they are  Salima Begum from Pakistan dahveed kaya  from Spain Rehman chambers from the  United Kingdom where Merson de Silva  Nogueira from Brazil Murray Chris  komari Jeremy from Germany Tracy and  Hall from Jamaica  Maggie MacDonell from the Canadian  Arctic  ken cylburn from Australia Michael Wow  Maya from Kenya and boy a young from  China congratulations to each of you  thank you for your hard work patience  and dedication and I want to say an  additional thank you to dedicated  teachers all over the world  you
 

